FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-wave-chamber.
OFF THE RECORD: Four frames of interference from two circular wave sources.
OFF THE RECORD: The scene computes distance and phase for every pixel.
OFF THE RECORD: A phase is an angle in the canon's 120-unit circle.

INCORPORATE BY REFERENCE statutes-of-trigonometry.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT wide IS 33.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 13.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT sines IS THE FINDING OF the-table-of-sines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ramp IS " .:-=+*#%@".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT phase IS 0.
ARTICLE 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS 0.
ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: Two horizontal cells span the height of one terminal cell.
    OFF THE RECORD: Positions use ten integer units per cell.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT py IS (2 TIMES row LESS (tall LESS 1)) TIMES 320 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 0.
ARTICLE 4.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT px IS (2 TIMES column LESS (wide LESS 1)) TIMES 160 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT wave IS THE FINDING OF interference REGARDING px AND py AND phase.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shade-index IS (wave PLUS 2000) TIMES 9 APPORTIONED AMONG 4000 PLUS 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS AN EXCERPT OF ramp FROM shade-index TO shade-index.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    SHOULD column FALL SHORT OF wide, REFER TO ARTICLE 4.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS "\n".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS 1.
    SHOULD row FALL SHORT OF tall, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    PROCLAIM frame.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT phase IS phase PLUS 30.
    SHOULD phase FALL SHORT OF 120, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

THE OFFICE OF wave-root, CONCERNING n.
    OFF THE RECORD: The floor of the square root, by Newton iteration.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 0, REMAND WITH 0.
    OFF THE RECORD: Keep the first Newton average safe even for large inputs.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS n APPORTIONED AMONG 2 PLUS 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: These exact square bounds reduce work for small inputs.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 65536, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS 256.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 256, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS 16.
    SHOULD n FAIL TO EXCEED 16, LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS 4.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-next IS (root-current PLUS n APPORTIONED AMONG root-current) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
SECTION 1.
    SHOULD root-next FAIL TO FALL SHORT OF root-current, REMAND WITH root-current.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-current IS root-next.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT root-next IS (root-current PLUS n APPORTIONED AMONG root-current) APPORTIONED AMONG 2.
    REFER TO SECTION 1.

THE OFFICE OF interference, CONCERNING x AND y AND clock-phase.
    OFF THE RECORD: Distances retain tenths of a cell through the square root.
    OFF THE RECORD: The sources are six cells from the center on each side.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left-distance IS THE FINDING OF wave-root REGARDING (x PLUS 60) TIMES (x PLUS 60) PLUS y TIMES y.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right-distance IS THE FINDING OF wave-root REGARDING (x LESS 60) TIMES (x LESS 60) PLUS y TIMES y.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT left-wave IS THE FINDING OF sine REGARDING left-distance TIMES 6 APPORTIONED AMONG 10 LESS clock-phase AND sines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT right-wave IS THE FINDING OF sine REGARDING right-distance TIMES 6 APPORTIONED AMONG 10 LESS clock-phase AND sines.
    REMAND WITH left-wave PLUS right-wave.
